// Major Image. L3: a vivid, lifelike phantom of an object, creature, or
// scene up to a large cube.
//
// Scope note (sound): the source spell also carries sound as part of its
// "fully sensory" illusion. Investigated whether that is reachable
// data-only, the same way minor_illusion_sound.ron's comment documents:
// `SoundEvent`/`SoundKind` is an AI-stimulus system, only reachable through
// a `BehaviorTree` node reading an `Agent` -- not available to a phantasm,
// which is `with_agent: false` by design. The other client-audible hook that
// exists, `Outcome::SummonedCreature`'s per-`Body` match in
// `voxygen/src/audio/sfx/mod.rs`, is hardcoded Rust covering a fixed list of
// specific existing monster/summon bodies, not a RON-selectable field --
// picking one of those bodies here just to piggyback its unrelated cue (a
// lantern hiss, a tornado swoosh) would fit the sound to the body rather
// than the body to the spell's own description, so that was rejected too. No
// data-only path (one-shot or looping) exists to attach real audio to an
// arbitrary phantasm body without new Rust. This RON ships the visual half
// only; the sound half is scoped out, same as minor_illusion_sound.ron.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.5,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: Object(TerracottaStatue),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        // Matches the compendium entry's Concentration(60) cap.
        duration: Some((
            secs: 60,
            nanos: 0,
        )),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
